{"name":"Roycroft Adobe","hex":"#a76251","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"adobe","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An unburnt brick dried in the sun.","The earth from which such bricks are made."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adobe"}],"entries":[{"title":"Roycroft","blocks":[{"text":"Roycroft was a reformist community of craft workers and artists which formed part of the Arts and Crafts movement in the United States. Elbert Hubbard founded the community in 1895, in the village of East Aurora, New York, near Buffalo. Participants were known as Roycrofters. The work and philosophy of the group, often referred to as the Roycroft movement, had a strong influence on the development of American architecture and design in the early 20th century."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Roycroft_Copper_Shop.jpg/330px-Roycroft_Copper_Shop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roycroft","wikidata":"Q2171198"},{"title":"Adobe","blocks":[{"text":"Adobe is a building material made from loam and organic materials. Adobe is Spanish for mudbrick. In some English-speaking regions of Spanish heritage, such as the Southwestern United States, the term is used to refer to any kind of earthen construction, or various architectural styles like Pueblo Revival or Territorial Revival. Most adobe buildings are similar in appearance to cob and rammed earth buildings. Adobe is among the earliest building materials, and is used throughout the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Adobe_wall_%28detail%29_1.jpg/330px-Adobe_wall_%28detail%29_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adobe","wikidata":"Q183496"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Roycroft_printing_press.jpg/500px-Roycroft_printing_press.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Roycroft_printing_press.jpg/1280px-Roycroft_printing_press.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Roycroft_printing_press.jpg/500px-Roycroft_printing_press.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Golding Pearl letterpress used by the Roycrofters","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARoycroft_printing_press.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/A_door_of_the_Chapel%2C_Roycroft_Campus.jpg/500px-A_door_of_the_Chapel%2C_Roycroft_Campus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/A_door_of_the_Chapel%2C_Roycroft_Campus.jpg/1280px-A_door_of_the_Chapel%2C_Roycroft_Campus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/A_door_of_the_Chapel%2C_Roycroft_Campus.jpg/500px-A_door_of_the_Chapel%2C_Roycroft_Campus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A door of the Chapel (not a religious building but a guild hall)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA_door_of_the_Chapel%2C_Roycroft_Campus.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Roycroft_Inn%2C_Lobby_bar%2C_Roycroft_Campus.jpg/500px-Roycroft_Inn%2C_Lobby_bar%2C_Roycroft_Campus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Roycroft_Inn%2C_Lobby_bar%2C_Roycroft_Campus.jpg/1280px-Roycroft_Inn%2C_Lobby_bar%2C_Roycroft_Campus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/t